Z||000015||Eric||06-04-2001||11:50 PM||||Roger, you don't want that car.  88s are the absolute worst cars to work on.  They have little poisonous snakes hidden thoughout the car.  If you remove a body panel, one's bound to strike at you.  I've been there...  I had to talk the snake down.  I said, "I'm just taking this fender off to get it fixed and painted."  Fortunatly he knew I lacked the funds to afford to put something "different" on my 88, so he scurried back into the space frame.<P>That car's just too nice.||||reg||1
Z||000016||rogergarrison||06-05-2001||12:03 AM||||Well I like Fieros mechanicly, even with thier quirks. Ive never been a fan of the body style personaly. I like exotics, but I like driving them, not paying the fortunes to fix them. This one is exactly what Im looking for, if the price is rite. Loaded, V6 automatic, that doesnt appear to need anything to interior or chassis. If it does go to $6K, i wont bid on it any further. If anyone close has got a great buy on another one similar, but any year let me know and youll 'save' this one. doesnt have to be a GT. I want everything else it has. I want to do the body only, dont want to mess with anything else, not even new plugs.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Eric||06-05-2001||10:31 AM||||Are you specifically looking for an 88 with a V6?||||reg||1
Z||000018||rogergarrison||06-05-2001||04:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>Are you specifically looking for an 88 with a V6?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>no, any year, any body style. factory installed V6, automatic, all options except sunroof. Body dont matter, but has to run perfect, nice (not mint) interior, any color. Everythings gotta work. Dont need any radio either. Has to be within a couple of hours of here to check it out. <P>I dont see why people knock down my wanting to do replicas. Should we be stuck with all the rolling junk that the rest of you dont want? I want a nice car too. Sorry if that sounds like a flame, I just had to get that off my chest. Not intended for anyone in particular. After all, its not like this GT is so special or rare. Theres thousands around and I want a NICE one.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||87GT||06-05-2001||04:30 PM||||Triad, it isnt my style at all but its gonna be your car so do what you want.  I am just voicing my opinion.  I do respect the time and work it takes to do kit cars, but I just am not a fan of doing it to fieros.  ||||reg||1
Z||000020||87GT||06-05-2001||04:33 PM||||Have any of you seen the Zimmer replica that was done on a fiero?  It was at the Daytona car show this past March.  The car took a lot of time and effort to convert on the owners part, but I just could not imagine that the owner thought the car was better looking than the fiero body it took place of.  I heard it was on a 88GT, but not sure.  Anybody see that car?  ugh!!||||reg||1
