Z||000024||kslish||06-08-2001||03:08 PM||||No offense Roger, but I really hope someone saves this one.  I guess I'm really defensive about '88s ever since a guy I know in Tampa, Fla. turned a silver '88 Formula (yes the rarest '88 Formula color) into a 355 replica.  I'm still crying over that one (however the front facia from that car is now on my coupe).  <P>Maybe if it was going to be another Ferrari body kit but those Fiero GT40 kits look strange, too out of proportion (although one day I'm going to build one of those tube frame GT40 replicas from scratch.  I already have the engine.)<P>As for TRiADS photoshopped pic...all is good, it still looks like a Fiero.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||rogergarrison||06-08-2001||09:59 PM||||well you can all rest, cause he wants too much for me to spend. The ERA GT 40 is excellent but the kit is way up there in the Viper price range. The Fiero kit can be made to look pretty decent with the top chopped a bit, and have to fabricate an upper door frame around the side windows so the doors have the cut out into the middle of the roof. If you really look, it is a little short, but the thing that really throws it off is how high the roof is, makes it really look short and high. After all, my cars are always drivers, not garage queens.||||reg||1
